{
  "id": 270173330,
  "iid": 13693,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Handle Quic Connection Migrations",
  "description": "Quic Connection Migrations are possible with zero length source\nconnection IDs. Currently, after connection migration Wireshark fails to\nassociate answers to the new address to the original connection.\nTherefor, it also fails to decrypt answers to the new IP.\n \nSo if a migration happens and the client sends data from the new IP\nthe connection data needs to be associated with the new conversation.\nSo when the server answers and the connection is identified by the\nconversation, a connection is found.\n\nSince I'm not really familiar with the Wireshark source code \nnor with all details from the quic rfcs. \nI'm really happy to get any feedback :smile:",
